data.content:
Your code **doesn't use `Thread.Abort`** at all. It only uses `Thread.Start()`, `Thread.Join()`, and `Thread.Sleep()` — all of which work identically in .NET 8 with no migration needed.

That said, for modern .NET, consider replacing raw threads with `Parallel.ForEach` or `Task.WhenAll` for cleaner batch processing:

```csharp
public async Task RunBatchAsync(List<WorkItem> items)
{
    await Parallel.ForEachAsync(items, async (item, ct) =>
    {
        await Task.Run(() => Process(item), ct);
    });
}
```

**Summary:** No `Thread.Abort` migration is required here — your code is already compatible with .NET 8 as-is.
